    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2F9bG3BeYczp4ntf5s3m69z)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main` (`55709cc`, after #498 and #502); needs nothing else, safe to merge anytime.\n- Conflicts with #503 (open) in a few lines of `sp-bibprocess` (doc and tangled `.el`): the `sp-bibtex-lint--kinds` list, `sp-bibtex--entry-rewrites`, the report in `sp-bibtex-lint--render`, `sp-bibtex-lint--follow`, `sp-bibtex-lint-convert`; and in the `L b f` keymap and its test in `sp-keys`. Keep both sides; the keys do not clash (`d`/`D` are #503, `u` is this PR).\n- After merging: if #503 merges first, merge `main` into this branch and keep both kinds; tangle `sp-academic.org` again.\n\n## What changed\n\nNew command `sp-bibtex-lint-fix-duplicates` (`C-; L b f u`): an entry with the same field twice is flagged first, and nothing is written until you apply.\n\n- Duplicate = same field name in one entry (case-insensitive); values compared without outer braces/quotes and with white space collapsed.\n- Identical copies: the report says so; the first copy is kept (safe).\n- Differing values: the report lists them numbered; you pick the value to keep for each field, or choose \"leave as it is\" to keep every copy. A differing value is never dropped without your pick.\n- Flow, like the other fixes: the command opens the report (`d`/`u`/`g`/`A`); `A` starts batches of `sp-bibtex-lint-batch-size`; each batch asks `a` apply (choose for each differing field), `i` identical copies only, `s` skip, `q` quit.\n- The file is copied to `sp-bibtex-lint-backup-directory` before the first write (restore by copying it back); an entry changed since the lint is left alone and counted.\n- Only the removed field lines change (the field with its comma, and its own line); the rest of the entry and its layout stay.\n- `sp-bibtex-lint-dryrun` has a \"Duplicate fields\" section and a button; `sp-bibtex-lint-convert` lists \"duplicate fields\".\n- Docs: section \"Duplicate fields\" in `sp-academic.org` (bullets); `L b f u` in `sp-keys.org`. No shims, `CHANGELOG.org` not edited.\n\n## Tests\n\n- 9 new tests in `tests/sp-bibprocess-lint-test.el` (scan and groups, resolve, one-line entry, report writes nothing, identical only, choose a value, leave as it is, skip, dry run report) and 1 in `tests/sp-keys-test.el` (tangled from `sp-keys.org`).\n- Emacs 29.3 in batch: 89 of 90 `sp-bibtex-*` tests pass; `sp-bibtex-lint-test-dryrun-report` fails the same way on `main`.\n- Not run on the real `.bib` files or on the Mac.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Pull this branch, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- [ ] On a copy of a real `.bib`, add `year = {2019},` twice to one entry and `year = {2019}` / `year = {2020}` to another\n- [ ] `C-; L b f u`: the report lists both entries; the identical one says \"identical copies\", the other lists \"1. 2019  2. 2020\"; the file is unchanged\n- [ ] `d` on one entry drops it from the fix; `u` brings it back\n- [ ] `A`, then `i`: only the identical copy is removed; the differing years are both still there; a backup exists in `sp-bibtex-lint-backup-directory`\n- [ ] Run again, `A`, `a`: you are asked which year to keep; the other line is removed and nothing else in the entry changes (`git diff`)\n- [ ] Choose \"leave as it is (keep every copy)\": that field is untouched\n- [ ] `s` and `q` at the batch question write nothing\n- [ ] A field with a different case (`Year`) counts as a duplicate of `year`\n- [ ] Regression: `C-; L b l` shows the new section and button; `C-; L b a` offers \"duplicate fields\"; `C-; L b f k` and `C-; L b f o` still work\n- [ ] Copy the backup over the `.bib` to restore it (untested by Claude on the real vault)\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard any local edits made while testing: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .` (and `git clean -fd` only after checking `git clean -nd`).\n- Return to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main` and `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`.\n- Optionally delete the test branch locally: `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D 504-bibtex-duplicate-fields`; the remote copy stays until the PR is merged or closed.\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`) so the config matches main again.\n- If the fix changed a `.bib` file, restore it from the backup folder the command reported (`sp-bibtex-lint-backup-directory`), or `git -C ~/Documents/bibliography restore .` if it is under git.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCARx5xrptvAbssfTb)_",
